{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 proof that for coprime m, d with d odd, and integers r1, r2 of multiplicative order exactly d modulo m with gcd(r_i - 1, m) = 1, if prod_{u=1}^{d-1} (xi^k - xi^{k r1^u})(xi^k - xi^{-k r1^u}) = prod_{u=1}^{d-1} (xi^k - xi^{k r2^u})(xi^k - xi^{-k r2^u}) for all integers k, where xi = exp(2 pi i/m), then r1^c = r2 mod m for some c, that is, r1 and r2 generate the same subgroup of (Z/m)^x. This proves the conjecture of MathOverflow question 503314 for every odd d and every m; the cases d an odd prime (Ikeda 1980) and (Z/m)^x cyclic (Colantonio and Lauret) were known. The identity comes from the spectra of lens spaces.",
  "authors": [
